# Disable autocrlf on generated files, they always generate with LF
# Add any extra files or paths here to make git stop saying they
# are changed when only line endings change.
src/generated/**/.cache/* text eol=lf
src/generated/**/*.json text eol=lf
# P7c: those two patterns carry "/" so they are anchored at the repository root and never
# match coe|cews|transmutation/src/generated/**. The module-side datagen output is written
# with LF as well (same providers, same DataProvider.saveStable), so repeat the rule per
# module; without it git warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF" once per file on every add.
coe/src/generated/**/*.json text eol=lf
cews/src/generated/**/*.json text eol=lf
transmutation/src/generated/**/*.json text eol=lf
# COE batch 6 (2026-10-04): line-ending root fix.  core.autocrlf=true alone leaves the text
# sources below unnormalised, so a fresh clone checks them out as CRLF, and every gate regex
# that anchors an end of line with "$" then goes FALSE-RED.  Measured on a fresh worktree:
#   - tools/check-armor-sets.ps1 section 29f "boomerang-family-helper" (boomerang\($ matched 0)
#   - tools/check-module-selfsufficiency.ps1 [[mods]] / [[mixins]] readers (a "`n" split keeps
#     the CR, and "(?:\s*#.*)?$" then matches no line at all)
# The regexes themselves now tolerate \r? as well (belt and braces); these rules keep the
# working tree LF in the first place.  *.json here subsumes the generated-json rules above.
# DELIBERATELY NOT COVERED: *.bat / *.ps1 / *.cmd (must stay CRLF, and they are local-only
# anyway) and every binary (e.g. textures *.png) -- forcing "text" on a binary would corrupt
# it on checkout.
*.java text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.mcmeta text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
